{"name":"Cressida","hex":"#8aae7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cressida","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Ancient Greek.","A moon of Uranus, Solar System."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cressida"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cressida","blocks":[{"text":"Cressida, also rendered Criseida, Cresseid or Criseyde, is a character who appears in many medieval and Renaissance-era retellings of the Trojan War, most notably Geoffrey Chaucer's Troilus and Criseyde and William Shakespeare's Troilus and Cressida. While her character in the later western tradition was developed from Chryseis, a minor figure in Homer's Iliad, they share few similarities."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Troilus_and_Cressida%2C_Act_I%2C_Scene_2_%2884341372%29.jpg/330px-Troilus_and_Cressida%2C_Act_I%2C_Scene_2_%2884341372%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cressida"},{"title":"Cressida (moon)","blocks":[{"text":"Cressida is an inner satellite of Uranus. It was discovered from the images taken by Voyager 2 on 9 January 1986, and was given the temporary designation S/1986 U 3. It was named after Cressida, the Trojan daughter of Calchas, a tragic heroine who appears in William Shakespeare's play Troilus and Cressida. It is also designated Uranus IX."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/93/Cressida_01-24-1986_V2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cressida_(moon)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Plate_13%2C_Cressida_%28E._J._Poynter%29_12000px.jpg/500px-Plate_13%2C_Cressida_%28E._J._Poynter%29_12000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Plate_13%2C_Cressida_%28E._J._Poynter%29_12000px.jpg/1280px-Plate_13%2C_Cressida_%28E._J._Poynter%29_12000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Plate_13%2C_Cressida_%28E._J._Poynter%29_12000px.jpg/500px-Plate_13%2C_Cressida_%28E._J._Poynter%29_12000px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Print, from a painting by E. J. Poynter, in The Graphic Gallery of Shakespeare's Heroines (1896)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlate_13%2C_Cressida_(E._J._Poynter)_12000px.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Cressida cressida 113360400","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Cressida_cressida_113360400.jpg/500px-Cressida_cressida_113360400.jpg","ratio":1.5021598272138228,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cressida_cressida_113360400.jpg","share":0.3075},{"title":"Cressida cressida 344787058","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Cressida_cressida_344787058.jpg/500px-Cressida_cressida_344787058.jpg","ratio":0.75,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cressida_cressida_344787058.jpg","share":0.148125},{"title":"Cressida cressida 177642301","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Cressida_cressida_177642301.jpg/500px-Cressida_cressida_177642301.jpg","ratio":0.47314453125,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cressida_cressida_177642301.jpg","share":0.124375},{"title":"Bali, Rice fields, Rice terraces in East Bali, Indonesia","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Bali%2C_Rice_fields%2C_Rice_terraces_in_East_Bali%2C_Indonesia.jpg/500px-Bali%2C_Rice_fields%2C_Rice_terraces_in_East_Bali%2C_Indonesia.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bali,_Rice_fields,_Rice_terraces_in_East_Bali,_Indonesia.jpg","share":0.094375},{"title":"Toyota Cressida Modified","image":"https://thumb.wi